femto patch for quireink-stardict 0.3.0
Subject: validate .ifo metadata instead of defaulting

Info::parse accepted any first line starting with the magic string, skipped
lines without '=', turned unparsable counts into 0, treated any
idxoffsetbits other than "64" as 32, and decoded the file lossily.

- Require the exact magic line, UTF-8 input and key=value lines.
- Reject duplicate known fields.
- Require version (2.4.2 or 3.0.0; 64-bit offsets only with 3.0.0),
  bookname, wordcount and idxfilesize; parse numbers strictly.
- Reject idxoffsetbits other than 32/64 and non-alphabetic
  sametypesequence values.
- Add Info::index_size and check it against the size of the .idx file.
- Reject a non-empty .syn file when synwordcount is absent or zero.

femto loads dictionaries copied by the user onto the device and wants
malformed files rejected at open rather than misread.

